questionvariables.text:
/*
Shared Curriculum-Independent
Question Bank

Linear Relations
QLIN-09

Licensed adaptation source:
NUMBAS-17290

Licence:
CC BY 4.0

The verified source provides the
straight-line graph family used as
the licensed adaptation basis.

The contextual service-plan scenario,
wording, generated parameters,
interpretation prompts and diagnostic
feedback in this STACK implementation
are independently written.
*/


/*
Choose a positive integer intersection
so both coordinates have meaningful
contextual interpretations.
*/

xI:rand(4)+2;


/*
Plan A has the steeper rate.

mA is between 4 and 6.
*/

mA:rand(3)+4;


/*
Plan B has a smaller positive rate.

This construction guarantees
mB < mA.
*/

mB:rand(mA-2)+1;


/*
Plan A begins with the lower fee.
*/

bA:rand(5)+2;


/*
Construct Plan B so that both plans
meet exactly when x=xI.

mA*xI+bA = mB*xI+bB
*/

bB:bA+(mA-mB)*xI;


/*
Common total cost at the intersection.
*/

yI:mA*xI+bA;


/*
Correct contextual interpretations.
*/

units:xI;

cost:yI;


/*
Diagnostic values.

These represent reversing the meanings
of the two coordinates.
*/

reversed_units:yI;

reversed_cost:xI;
